      "text": "System architecture is the high-level structural decomposition of a system — what the major elements are, how they are connected, and which design principles govern the whole. Architecture decisions are the most consequential and most expensive to change. Getting them right early is the leverage point of SE."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-ARCHITECTURE.md#003",
